<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Calpurnius Piso the Pontifex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">48 BCE–32 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Lucius Calpurnius Piso Pontifex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Calpurnius Piso the Pontifex was a Roman senator and general, consul in 15 BCE. From about 13 to 11 BCE he fought a hard campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> against the Bessi and other tribes who had risen against the Roman client king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhoemetalces-i">Rhoemetalces I</a>, for which he received triumphal honours. He later served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> for many years as prefect of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucius-calpurnius-piso-the-pontifex.jpg" alt="Lucius Calpurnius Piso the Pontifex" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L_Calpurnius_Piso_Pontifex_MAN_Napoli_Inv5601.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
